     "comparison": "Halcyon accepts an 8% S2 permanent limit, above the acceptable max 5%, while S5 remains weakened to discretionary review rather than mandatory recall, benefiting Halcyon.",
     "status": "carried_out",
     "excerpt": "A model must not exceed an 8% failure rate. Any result above 8% requires prompt submission of a corrective-action plan to the regulator and retesting within 6 months; regulators may restrict sales if the model remains above 8%. Individual per-model failure rates must be provided to customers who buy that model, including prospective customers before purchase; public disclosure is not required."
