    "notice_days": "immediate",
    "serious_injury_recall": null,
    "quote": "Customers must receive clear, model-specific safety notices promptly when a manufacturer or regulator identifies a material safety risk, including known hazards, affected units, immediate precautions, and available remedies. A rate above 8 thermal incidents per 100,000 installed units in a year requires prompt regulator review and a public determination of whether recall or other protective action is necessary; it does not by itself automatically trigger a recall."
